1578
02:27:20,238 --> 02:27:21,252
Why this matters?

1579
02:27:21,998 --> 02:27:29,828
For most of human history, turning an idea into a visual required either deep skill, expensive tools, or both.

1580
02:27:31,022 --> 02:27:37,124
A filmmaker needed a crew, a designer needed years of training, a marketer needed a budget.

1581
02:27:38,158 --> 02:27:41,508
AI image and video generation begins to change that.

1582
02:27:42,062 --> 02:27:48,260
It moves creative power from the hands of the few to anyone with an idea and the words to describe it.

1583
02:27:48,878 --> 02:27:51,716
These tools don't replace artists or filmmakers.

1584
02:27:52,526 --> 02:28:02,212
Skilled human creativity still produces work that AI cannot, but they do give everyone else a seat at the creative table that simply wasn't available before.

1585
02:28:02,478 --> 02:28:13,540
And as these tools continue to mature technically, legally, and ethically, understanding both their power and their boundaries is what makes you not just a capable user,

1586
02:28:13,902 --> 02:28:15,172
but a responsible one.

1587
02:28:15,502 --> 02:28:20,324
Use additional tools like deep research, create image, and agent mode.

1588
02:28:21,262 --> 02:28:23,524
Here's a question worth sitting with for a moment.

1589
02:28:24,110 --> 02:28:28,068
When you first started using Chat GPT, what did you use it for?

1590
02:28:29,102 --> 02:28:35,876
Probably something like answering a question, drafting an email, maybe summarizing a document, and it was useful.

1591
02:28:36,238 --> 02:28:44,164
But at some point, you might have hit a wall, a moment where you thought, I wish this could just go find the latest information for me,

1592
02:28:44,590 --> 02:28:50,884
or I wish I could see this as a visual, or I wish I didn't have to guide it step by step through every part of this task.

1593
02:28:52,142 --> 02:28:54,916
Here's the thing: those capabilities exist.

1594
02:28:56,014 --> 02:28:58,308
They are built into ChatGPT right now.

1595
02:28:58,798 --> 02:29:00,708
Most people just don't know they are there.

1596
02:29:01,518 --> 02:29:02,852
Or how to turn them on.

1597
02:29:04,014 --> 02:29:12,388
Now we are going to walk through three tools that transform Chat GPT from a text assistant into something significantly more powerful.

1598
02:29:13,294 --> 02:29:18,436
The first one is the deep research for when you need true current multi-source intelligence.

1599
02:29:18,894 --> 02:29:29,476
Create image for when you need to see an idea, not just read about it, and we also have agent mode when you want to hand over a goal and let AI figure out these steps.

1600
02:29:30,670 --> 02:29:37,988
By the end of this session, you will know exactly what each tool does, when to use it, and how to get started step by step.

1601
02:29:38,702 --> 02:29:41,156
Let's dive deeper into each of these tools now.

1602
02:29:42,574 --> 02:29:44,164
The first tool is deep research.

1603
02:29:44,686 --> 02:29:45,284
What is it?

1604
02:29:45,774 --> 02:29:46,692
Why does it matter?

1605
02:29:47,726 --> 02:29:49,188
Let's start with a scenario.

1606
02:29:49,614 --> 02:29:57,728
You want to understand how the European Union's new AI regulations compare with what's happening in the United States, the United Kingdom,

1607
02:29:58,030 --> 02:29:59,620
and other countries around the world.

1608
02:30:00,014 --> 02:30:09,220
It's a fast-changing topic, politics are being updated regularly, and you need a clear, well-structured answer, not just a surface-level paragraph.

1609
02:30:10,126 --> 02:30:16,548
If you type that into a standard Chat GPT session, you will get a response based on what the model learned.

1610
02:30:17,934 --> 02:30:24,804
During this training, the information might be several months old, it won't reflect last week's policy announcement,

1611
02:30:25,102 --> 02:30:31,332
and it will typically draw from a single thread of reasoning rather than comparing across multiple current sources.

1612
02:30:32,622 --> 02:30:34,852
Deep research changes that entirely.

1613
02:30:35,726 --> 02:30:39,972
Deep research in ChatGPTS Advanced Web Intelligence feature.

1614
02:30:40,590 --> 02:30:50,448
Instead of relying only on its training data, it actively goes out to the Internet, runs multiple searches in sequence, pulls information from several sources,

1615
02:30:50,768 --> 02:30:56,388
analyzes what it finds, and then synthesizes everything into a comprehensive structured response.

1616
02:30:57,486 --> 02:30:58,884
Think of the difference like this.

1617
02:30:59,758 --> 02:31:08,100
A standard Chat GPT reply is like asking a knowledgeable colleague a question and getting their best answer off the top of their head.

1618
02:31:09,070 --> 02:31:18,020
Deep research is like asking that same colleague to go away for a few minutes, read four to five recent articles on the topic, cross-reference them,

1619
02:31:18,286 --> 02:31:20,836
and come back with the properly structured briefing.

1620
02:31:21,838 --> 02:31:29,700
The second answer takes a little longer, but the quality, depth, and accuracy of information are in a completely different league.

1621
02:31:30,414 --> 02:31:34,404
That makes deep research particularly valuable for academic work.

1622
02:31:34,798 --> 02:31:38,660
Researching a topic where you need multiple perspectives and recent sources,

1623
02:31:39,438 --> 02:31:48,260
professional decisions, understanding market trends, regulatory changes, competitor landscapes, fast-moving fields,

1624
02:31:48,688 --> 02:31:55,844
technology, science, global news, where what was true six months ago may already be outdated.

1625
02:31:56,462 --> 02:32:03,172
Comparative analysis when you need to evaluate options, frameworks, or positions side by side.

1626
02:32:03,662 --> 02:32:05,284
How to use it step by step.

1627
02:32:05,806 --> 02:32:07,844
The first step is to enable the feature.

1628
02:32:08,302 --> 02:32:16,484
Go to the settings, tools, and make sure deep research is turned on. It won't appear as an option in your chat unless it's enabled.

1629
02:32:17,262 --> 02:32:20,164
Step two, ask a substantive question.

1630
02:32:20,782 --> 02:32:24,676
Deep research works best when you give it a question with some depth to it.

1631
02:32:25,134 --> 02:32:35,268
Not just what is AI, but something like how do EU AI regulations in 2025 compare with US, UK, and global AI governance frameworks.

1632
02:32:36,366 --> 02:32:41,444
The more specific and layered your question is, the more value deep research delivers.

1633
02:32:42,830 --> 02:32:43,556
Step 3.

1634
02:32:44,014 --> 02:32:44,804
Let it work.

1635
02:32:45,966 --> 02:32:52,004
Chat GPT will begin searching, cross-referencing multiple sources, and building its response.

1636
02:32:52,846 --> 02:32:56,164
You will often see it working through the process in real time.

1637
02:32:56,942 --> 02:33:00,740
This takes longer than a standard reply, and that's expected.

1638
02:33:01,134 --> 02:33:03,108
It's doing significantly more work.

1639
02:33:04,142 --> 02:33:07,684
Then is your step four, review your synthesized report.

1640
02:33:08,206 --> 02:33:10,180
The output won't just be a paragraph.

1641
02:33:10,670 --> 02:33:21,380
It will typically be a structured multi-section response with context, comparisons, and sourced insights, the kind of output that would take you significant time to compile manually.

1642
02:33:22,030 --> 02:33:23,044
What to keep in mind?

1643
02:33:23,406 --> 02:33:25,700
It requires a plus plan or higher.

1644
02:33:26,894 --> 02:33:29,508
Deep research is not available on the free trial.

1645
02:33:30,350 --> 02:33:34,020
Some advanced research capabilities may be limited to enterprise accounts.

1646
02:33:34,990 --> 02:33:36,548
Check the current plan details.

1647
02:33:37,454 --> 02:33:43,492
Deep research availability and the plans it's included in have changed over time and continue to evolve.

1648
02:33:44,750 --> 02:33:51,140
At the time of recording, access was available on paid plans, but OpenAI updates these policies regularly.

1649
02:33:51,918 --> 02:34:02,468
Before assuming you do or don't have access, check settings tools in your Chat GPT interface or visit OpenAI's current plan comparison page for the most accurate information.

1650
02:34:03,246 --> 02:34:06,244
Don't rely solely on what you see in a course or article.

1651
02:34:07,150 --> 02:34:09,220
Plan features is the space more quickly.

1652
02:34:09,582 --> 02:34:13,700
It's slower by design, but it's searching and analyzing in real time.

1653
02:34:14,478 --> 02:34:16,964
Responses take longer than a regular reply.

1654
02:34:17,486 --> 02:34:19,172
This is normal and expected.

1655
02:34:19,566 --> 02:34:21,668
It cannot access paywalled content.

1656
02:34:22,222 --> 02:34:27,236
If a source requires a subscription to read, deep research can't get behind that wall.

1657
02:34:27,694 --> 02:34:30,244
It works with publicly available information.

1658
02:34:30,862 --> 02:34:38,660
In summaries rather than quotes, you will get synthesized insights and paraphrased content, not verbatim extracts from articles.

1659
02:34:39,246 --> 02:34:47,428
This is both a feature because it integrates information rather than just copying it, and a limitation to be aware of when you need direct citations.

1660
02:34:48,654 --> 02:34:50,416
Tool two is create image.

1661
02:34:50,830 --> 02:34:52,580
What is it and why does it matter?

